Z||000000||AL||01-16-2000||08:24 PM||||<BR>ok guys this is my question, i took apart my motors, 4 to be exact,2 had perfect gears so i cleaned out all the old grease and put in new grease. i put them back together and the drivers side goes up and down perfect, the other one only goes down and not up, i changed the relays and still the same. so my question is why doesn't the left side go up when it has perfect gears in it, and the switch inside is good.AL.||||reg||5
Z||000001||862M4inCA||01-17-2000||01:54 AM||||Check to see that you have +12V coming from the blue wire going to the motor when you're lights are in the off position (This is the wire with the quick disconnect wire). That wire should only have voltage when the light switch is in the off position. If it doesn't I'd check the relay which is located on the left fender by the left headlight motor. You might have a bad wire connection somewhere between the motor and there.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||01-17-2000||06:15 AM||||When you checked the limit switch inside the motor did you do a continuity check of the wire leads to the contacts?  On one of my motors there was a loose connection where one of the leads was crimped to the limit switch.  It had enough connection to satisfy the continuity test with a digital volt/ohm meter but was loose enough not to be able to carry adequate current to run the motor.  I soldered the wire into the crimp connector and all was better.<P>Hope this helps,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000003||AL||01-17-2000||10:31 PM||||yes i checked every thing, i even cleaned the contacts, and where it makes contact, i even checked for power and all is good, the only thing is it doesn't go up, bt it goes down ver good. i guess i will be taking it apart again. thanks guys, AL.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Spyder||01-17-2000||10:49 PM||||I had a similar problem, mine was the interior switch. I had to push it to the side to make it work.<p>[This message has been edited by Spyder (edited 01-17-2000).]||||reg||1
