Z||000013||DRH||01-22-2000||04:32 AM||||Al,<P>In case William doesn't make it out into the snow. I didn't feel like going out in below 0 to look at the 84 but I did pull out my Haynes manual with wiring diagrams. If I am looking at the correct connectors there should be 4 on the left (2 pink, black and red) and 3 on the right (pink, black and red). The 2 pink on the left should go to the same terminal, one is incoming power for open and the other runs to the right motor.<P>If the left motor will go down but not up regardless of motor and relay used...<BR>Check for power on the Red wire at the left relay. It should be hot at all times. That wire comes from fusible link C, the right red wire comes from fusible link D. If it's not, most likely cause is bad fusible link C or a bad connection in that wire somewhere. <P>On my 88 (in the garage, not quite so cold   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) the fusible links are 2 reddish-orange wires that loop out of the wire harness that runs under the brake master cylinder out to the headlights. Yours should be similar. Unfortunately I don't know exactly how to fix it (replace the bad part of the wire ???)<P>GM seems to have gone out of the way to make each headlight's up function independent; seperate relays, seperate power. The down uses only the isolation relay and the tail light fused power. Safety issue maybe???<P>Good luck, David.<p>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 01-22-2000).]||||reg||1
