Z||000015||Monkeyman||01-22-2000||04:29 PM||||Al--What year is your car?  '84-'86 motors were different than '87-'88.  If you have the older gen motors, DRHs info might not help much (sorry, DRH--at least you tried).  I'm not sure what the difference was but if you ever get the money to change over to the later style, do it.  They are quieter with less hassles and <B>MUCH</B> cheaper to rebuild<B>!!!</B>||||reg||1
Z||000016||AL||01-22-2000||07:08 PM||||ok guys i traced the wires and no current going thru at all, i then cut the switchand put in a new wire from the other motor to the other switch, presto it worked perfectly and now both go up and down(like a whore)lol perfectly. so that takes care of that, buy the way bill i went to the junkyard this morning and took two motors outof a TA, i then got under the car and took my portable drill and drilled both motors, to my surprise two perfect aluminum gears, i was estatic. so bill the weather over here is a good74 degrees. i had to rub it a little, thanks to all the fiero brothers for your help, no more headlight topics forever, right bill, AL ||||reg||6
